The minor in which a hub works on one machine, proofs and arguments read what they actually rest on, and replies fit the budget they are asked for. It carries:
- #785-#788 (P7, a hub on one machine): tracked search from committed exports, a composed check over a hub and several designs, computed seams, import_graph merge, upstream_status reviewed revisions, a link whose far node is gone;
- #789: rmcp 3.6.0, its new line bound lifted on stdio and the --call pipe;
- #790 (PR A1): bridge premises, EQUIVALENT_TO, circular steps, a proof read as a proof whatever its domain, contested through a contested contradiction, a what-if through falsum;
- #791 (PR A2): claimed, withdrawn and superseded readings; not_read and graded sources; a refreshed mirror keeps what its source withdraws; independence compares premises; unsourced objections contest only;
- #792 (PR B): replies fit (premise_whys, hub budgets, get_skill and propagate_from budget_chars, compact --call output);
- the cut itself (release/v0.91.0).

Pinned here: rel:v0910, the increment's ChangeEvents (found by diffing ids against the v0.90.0 tag's committed copy), and the cut's drift acceptances. Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Xbw6PG9mXJiU2Sb421fnq
